ou to do interesting things  so how the game plays we played on this  Anaya palace map they're trying to get  rid of the three lane design and they're  trying to make the game focused around  what they call power points what they  really mean are basically buildings you  controlling buildings the palace map  played really interesting there's a  central Palace as it is in the name and  there's a courtyard and we had a couple  of matches where the one team or the  other controlled that courtyard and the  entrance points to that court you are  really well and that made a huge  difference in that match so that's where  the new killstreak system is very  important and also our big team battle  continues to be exciting for me so you  tend to break those stalemates with  killstreaks I drove around in a tank for  a while which was a you know something  that was in I believe World War two but  it's a killstreak this time around and  it's crazy to think you know I'm  suddenly driving a tank around in a big  team battle mode in Call of Duty the  white phosphorus which everybody's been  kind of talking about a lot it's  actually very useful in this mode  because if an enemy team is holding that  courtyard and you just simply can't  break through you know the white  phosphorus has a mechanic it actually  blankets the whole area of the map and  starts choking the enemy team and it  makes it easier for your team to move  into that area  I think big team battle brings a lot of  meaning and purpose to your weapon  builds your overall load outs and your  kill streaks that you take with you  there's also things like something like  a tactical insertion flare which becomes  now more important because on a bigger  map you need to choose where you spawn  grenade interceptor just because there's  more people throwing grenades the  overall feel of big team battle was it's  oddly Call of Duty feeling just because  there's so many people on the map at  once doing so many kill streaks and so 